<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">2001</h1><p class="ref-lede">2001 in world history: 11 events, 13 deaths, 1 work, 1 state founded and 2 that came to an end. 188 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1997">1997</a><a href="/years/1998">1998</a><a href="/years/1999">1999</a><a href="/years/2000">2000</a><a href="/years/2001" aria-current="page">2001</a><a href="/years/2002">2002</a><a href="/years/2003">2003</a><a href="/years/2004">2004</a><a href="/years/2005">2005</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-11">11 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Timothy McVeigh is executed for the Oklahoma City bombing</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">McVeigh was put to death by lethal injection in Terre Haute, Indiana. It was the first federal execution in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> since 1963.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-11">11 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Al-Qaeda's September 11 attacks kill 2,977 people</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hijackers crashed airliners into the World Trade Center and the Pentagon; a fourth plane came down in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>. The attacks killed 2,977 people and led to the US-led wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-7">7 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The US and Britain begin air strikes on Afghanistan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American and British forces began bombing Taliban and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda">al-Qaeda</a> targets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, four weeks after the 11 September attacks. The war toppled the Taliban but lasted nearly twenty years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-15">15 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Leaning Tower of Pisa reopens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After eleven years of closure and stabilisation work, the Leaning Tower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> reopened to visitors. Engineers had reduced its tilt by about 44 centimetres, securing it for centuries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-20">20 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Argentina's president resigns amid riots</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-de-la-rua">Fernando de la Rúa</a> resigned and fled the Casa Rosada by helicopter as protests over economic collapse left dozens dead. Days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> declared the largest sovereign default to that date.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bonn-agreement-2001">Bonn Agreement (2001)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bonn Agreement was signed on 5 December 2001 in Bonn, Germany, by Afghan factions opposed to the Taliban under United Nations auspices.</p></div></li></ol></section>
